  "claimVersions": [
    {
      "id": "claim-version:fad8c500-9ffd-49e7-b6a3-8b4f8c0d1fda",
      "claimId": "claim:8fdf6206-7cc5-414c-af95-d5836195bad6",
      "targetVersionId": "target-version:76e9dd83-3247-4599-9260-572210e5154d",
      "anchor": {
        "file": "paper/Generating_Antichains_Simplified.tex",
        "excerptDigest": "sha256-cac2be97fead5a3bb0d7c3375ea794aa86feb3c519bc040775eadaad774f331f"
      },
      "text": "There exist absolute C > 0 and an integer n_0 such that alpha(n) <= C f(n) for every integer n >= n_0.",
      "normalizedTextDigest": "sha256-0ee0f64c9749e18e8229f7bc458626ba5c060d252221f661b113a24568ee75b7",
      "kind": "other",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "file": "paper/Generating_Antichains_Simplified.tex",
          "excerptDigest": "sha256-cac2be97fead5a3bb0d7c3375ea794aa86feb3c519bc040775eadaad774f331f"
        }
      ],
      "status": "active"
    },
    {
      "id": "claim-version:21bb8fa0-0286-4f18-a058-80af0a93298a",
      "claimId": "claim:8f5bead0-1ac7-47a5-b6ad-f1bac17870ea",
      "targetVersionId": "target-version:76e9dd83-3247-4599-9260-572210e5154d",
      "anchor": {
        "file": "paper/Generating_Antichains_Simplified.tex",
        "excerptDigest": "sha256-0a5ae3c243a3c2ed317f9ba5fdfdf7fb64edd7f1790d9ab45185836bc8f7a16a"
      },
      "text": "For an absolute c > 0, the integers n >= 5 with c f(n) <= alpha(n) have natural density 1; c is chosen independently of all n and cutoffs.",
      "normalizedTextDigest": "sha256-1c1731480db8b68caa37e3da3b1fb1c7c7e0da9523045662da3e99b13664976f",
      "kind": "other",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "file": "paper/Generating_Antichains_Simplified.tex",
          "excerptDigest": "sha256-0a5ae3c243a3c2ed317f9ba5fdfdf7fb64edd7f1790d9ab45185836bc8f7a16a"
        }
      ],
      "status": "active"
    },
    {
      "id": "claim-version:d20f4f47-31a0-4adf-a44a-ca8bfae89922",
      "claimId": "claim:25a5918c-8c7e-4f3d-a084-b241bd3f72c2",
      "targetVersionId": "target-version:76e9dd83-3247-4599-9260-572210e5154d",
      "anchor": {
        "file": "paper/Generating_Antichains_Simplified.tex",
        "excerptDigest": "sha256-6b54bd9ec2d366111231d9cc67ab5af533b656ed330ee4137fb143e11ace70eb"
      },
      "text": "For fixed positive absolute c and C, the simultaneous inequalities c f(n) <= alpha(n) <= C f(n) hold on a set of positive integers of natural density 1.",
      "normalizedTextDigest": "sha256-8abac860e4601a81ae15f743c8b76700f9d71ed82c888b616554c8f294eed152",
      "kind": "other",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "file": "paper/Generating_Antichains_Simplified.tex",
          "excerptDigest": "sha256-6b54bd9ec2d366111231d9cc67ab5af533b656ed330ee4137fb143e11ace70eb"
        }
      ],
      "status": "active"
    },
    {
      "id": "claim-version:22e56616-e423-4d70-9d62-4412be3ba6b4",
      "claimId": "claim:4115e09b-29c4-440b-9c58-a25b96884368",
      "targetVersionId": "target-version:76e9dd83-3247-4599-9260-572210e5154d",
      "anchor": {
        "file": "paper/Generating_Antichains_Simplified.tex",
        "excerptDigest": "sha256-5b658bb96f2b48856711539e40bc7b7cf0416b75e7fc36ae7bc7b02dc3bf0845"
      },
      "text": "There exist a,A > 0 and X_0 > 4 such that a f(X) <= max_{1<=n<X} alpha(n) <= A f(X) for every real X >= X_0.",
      "normalizedTextDigest": "sha256-36be4d2d59be34269c70bc811e77b8d2d9713b9a10014bfc44885cfdc6843622",
      "kind": "other",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "file": "paper/Generating_Antichains_Simplified.tex",
          "excerptDigest": "sha256-5b658bb96f2b48856711539e40bc7b7cf0416b75e7fc36ae7bc7b02dc3bf0845"
        }
      ],
      "status": "active"
    },
    {
      "id": "claim-version:66b057a5-a4c6-410e-a114-3e1eddefcb4c",
      "claimId": "claim:89584538-91d7-4928-9763-b49835ef71f5",
      "targetVersionId": "target-version:76e9dd83-3247-4599-9260-572210e5154d",
      "anchor": {
        "file": "paper/Generating_Antichains_Simplified.tex",
        "excerptDigest": "sha256-9064ca3024f84b0407a3343651d58921cede604d81d40b37340ed99fdf2aa359"
      },
      "text": "For X >= 0, realGoodInputs c C X consists exactly of the integers n with 5 <= n <= X satisfying both non-strict bounds.",
      "normalizedTextDigest": "sha256-bb1e9da3d668ff232e552f2c2de5ad1582a02ac861d2cafe5f223d1ce8143537",
      "kind": "correctness",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "file": "paper/Generating_Antichains_Simplified.tex",
          "excerptDigest": "sha256-9064ca3024f84b0407a3343651d58921cede604d81d40b37340ed99fdf2aa359"
        }
      ],
      "status": "active"
    },
    {
      "id": "claim-version:ac76fa41-a175-4a10-98f9-c2bb86c82c75",
      "claimId": "claim:a14c1072-8c6e-47fa-8e62-d44b8448f686",
      "targetVersionId": "target-version:76e9dd83-3247-4599-9260-572210e5154d",
      "anchor": {
        "file": "paper/Generating_Antichains_Simplified.tex",
        "excerptDigest": "sha256-4aec5e33bb24fb13d9e96a9b86509dc54742000a653670c742f206c809053865"
      },
      "text": "A density-zero count of orderExceptions is equivalent to the density-one goodInputs proportion, and the natural-cutoff good proportion gives the same real-cutoff proportion.",
      "normalizedTextDigest": "sha256-7e5ac43d28a3272ac013b3c70e226e6acb4f3cc8a656110f52e0d71522f9900e",
      "kind": "correctness",
